<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump absent as New York marks 25 years since 9/11 with first Muslim mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16a81de7fa8991f438769368aa0c6de4df61e371e7e1c654069a609a562d168d</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor--1ab77d9771b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor" /><summary type="html">New York marks the 25th anniversary of the Sept. 11 attacks on Friday, with President Donald Trump attending a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents join commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e57a0dc4ce0e8f9bbd055620d942c951f9131fd6950ad1d9a39ceed2a9304cc</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:11:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1--ff193be16a97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1" /><summary type="html">Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1077818961e451d138ebaba56ac1d95502aef025e3145fb0c16735820dd087b</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks--138f5fff2da5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>9/11 then and now: Do September 2001 attacks still shape our world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a44dcc636b9cc533b7f53e7389010813d23df1d6ea3edca27d91bb7c6ec894d1</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world--b22b4497a9ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world" /><summary type="html">Once in a generation, sometimes once in a lifetime, a singular event blindsides the entire planet. 25 years on, does the memory of the Nine-Eleven attacks against New York's Twin Towers, the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania fade into history or is it still as raw and vivid as on that sunny September morning?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about Trump's pledge of $5,000 to 'every American' if GOP wins midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98130832557b7452c35033b2cc21ac8b571157ea4e4f14f2a0eb3ec8b6b3500b</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:39:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge--bf5bef619ba0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump ⁠promised a $5,000 "Trump dividend" ​payment to every US adult on Wednesday if his Republicans retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in the November 3 midterm elections. The pledge has raised numerous questions. Here's what we know so far.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Montserrat: The 'Pompeii' of the Caribbean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6c9ee340a86c5f1015380465ae78a69847c1b7f370438a46887eefd7a305bea</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:58:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260910-montserrat-the-pompeii-of-the-caribbean--7253ab857f62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260910-montserrat-the-pompeii-of-the-caribbean" /><summary type="html">Part of the island of Montserrat, a UK Overseas Territory, was buried by a volcanic eruption in 1995. Today, caution is essential for those venturing on the mysterious island that is full of spectacular Caribbean landscapes. Our colleagues at France Télévisions and FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Colombia court orders President de la Espriella to hide social media videos of him with dead bodies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e836a501604d3564756aba85123b5204a790b19c553a70616efe3f3e81ffdc9</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T11:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-colombia-court-orders-president-de-la-espriella-to-hide-social-media-videos-of-him-with-dea--dd0eaf06ad37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-colombia-court-orders-president-de-la-espriella-to-hide-social-media-videos-of-him-with-dead-bodies" /><summary type="html">Colombia's right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella has been ordered to hide social media videos showing him walking past rows of the dead bodies of alleged guerrillas killed by the country's armed forces, according to a court document seen Wednesday. The newly sworn-in president has launched a fresh offensive at armed groups involved in the country's lucrative cocaine trade.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Egomaniac': Papers discuss 'Trumpapalooza' midterm convention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbad146a9b2998e0fd46082e84b78afc9f9156feaf391af2e9f1efee37e0f7d5</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/egomaniac-papers-discuss-trumpapalooza-midterm-convention--59197c706a94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/egomaniac-papers-discuss-trumpapalooza-midterm-convention" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 10: US papers react to the first night of the Republicans' midterm convention in Dallas. Also: five baby orangutans from Southeast Asia have been found in a forest in India. Then some dystopian science news. Finally, perhaps we don't need to do as much sport as we think we do.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump can see the writing on the wall here': Republicans hold midterm convention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e1eed54469686a922c01be6ec89bd71a3904d7e00c1234878d091d3d5f682c9</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:39:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-can-see-the-writing-on-the-wall-here-republicans-hold-midterm-convention--ab7613fbd6ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-can-see-the-writing-on-the-wall-here-republicans-hold-midterm-convention" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24's Washington, DC correspondent Fraser Jackson weighs in on US President Donald Trump's efforts to leverage his fading star power to help the Republican Party hold onto Congress in November's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>How a former BAPS temple worker in the US got his freedom, but still seeks justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:183e8210bdc1b3acef2c82f851f7b448f39c59b092ffa9c7091de36bd4ab4524</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:37:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-how-a-former-baps-temple-worker-in-the-us-got-his-freedom-but-still-seeks-justice--2b4216bb60c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-how-a-former-baps-temple-worker-in-the-us-got-his-freedom-but-still-seeks-justice" /><summary type="html">The Bochasanwasi Akshar Purushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS) Hindu sect at the heart of the Eiffel Tower strike made headlines in France during the inauguration of its latest temple near Paris. In the US, BAPS came under the spotlight when Indian stone workers were rescued from a temple construction site. One former worker recounts his journey and fight for justice.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he'll give Americans $5,000 each if Republicans win midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60cd7b9ebf3d29dfeb466d43195e6ffd45f9c2f0849fcd9fa48d4db5ac62d282</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:15:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-trump-says-give-americans-5-000-each-if-republicans-win-midterm-elections--4c62fe7d9fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-trump-says-give-americans-5-000-each-if-republicans-win-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Wednesday urged his supporters to pretend he was on the ballot in the upcoming midterm elections in November, even saying he would give $5,000 to each American adult if the right-wing Republicans maintain control of Congress. Trump is struggling with low opinion ratings as the cost of living soars and his months-long war against Iran drags on.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil Supreme Court chief suspends colleagues' rulings amid election row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0639a3c4989300e30fe98a84907c2c4ce73c64417aeef4157f823aa8b9488a74</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T23:44:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-brazil-supreme-court-chief-suspends-rival-rulings-amid-election-row--feb36b8c119c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-brazil-supreme-court-chief-suspends-rival-rulings-amid-election-row" /><summary type="html">The chief justice of Brazil's Supreme Court stepped in Wednesday to halt conflicting rulings by two fellow judges as a dispute over alleged links between Justice Alexandre de Moraes and a banker accused of fraud deepened. The clash has spilled into the campaign for next month's presidential election, adding to tensions around the court.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio to seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e1a8c2f8554253de9acdacdfb4c39c77eb739125f0fb6f1999350d1048701bb</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T22:58:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-to-seek-45-million-in-additional-security-funding-for-ecuador--4e3ac603990e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-to-seek-45-million-in-additional-security-funding-for-ecuador" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Wednesday that Washington would seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador and provide military equipment as the two countries deepen cooperation against drug trafficking. During a visit to Quito, Rubio also announced new sanctions on former Ecuadorian officials involved in bribery and a terrorist designation for an Ecuador-based gang.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump 'believes in the power of his own charisma', analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abce8d08f0b056a2071789c0b5a8080b7af92c1a8d49e596ac94f3b9ba1b1ec9</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T21:09:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260909-trump-believes-in-the-power-of-his-own-charisma-analyst-says--6c00269de42d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260909-trump-believes-in-the-power-of-his-own-charisma-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">Republicans opened their highly unusual midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday afternoon, a “Trump-a-Palooza” that is putting the president at the centre of this fall’s midterm elections – whether the candidates running like it or not. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Professor Todd Belt, Director of the Political Management Programme at George Washington University, says that Trump "believes in the power of his own charisma".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Trump claims firefighters carried him to safety ‘right after’ 9/11, but his account is disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec2073524b9a6dbaaf694025157289a11da0626123bd4a466f55753b798d8ecc</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T20:52:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-claims-firefighters-carried-him-to-safety-right-after-9-11-but-his-account-is-disputed-1--27acdb9ff2f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-claims-firefighters-carried-him-to-safety-right-after-9-11-but-his-account-is-disputed-1" /><summary type="html">As the 25th anniversary of 9/11 approaches, US President Donald Trump has lashed out at the press over coverage questioning where he was. This week, he said two firefighters carried him to safety near the US Steel Building right after the attacks, though he later said that he wasn’t at the World Trade Center on the day of the collapse. His version of events and alleged role at Ground Zero have evolved many times over the years. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Republicans put Trump center stage in US midterms gamble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77328b0b7937c1c091e3476b6bc46bfc895a7e6e98a1aba889ef2f772cb94df0</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble--87590ae3ef88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble" /><summary type="html">US Republicans open an extraordinary midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday betting that putting Donald Trump at the center of their campaign can rescue a party facing grim election forecasts -- despite the president's deeply negative approval ratings. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>How a French Foreign Legion soldier dramatically escaped Colombian captors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44042060ec6ccb9701baa06d09c47228da5eca6814649c7eb85a57ed25b2a70b</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:17:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors--eda72903bbbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors" /><summary type="html">A French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrillas escaped after nearly a month in captivity by overpowering a guard, jumping into a river with his hands tied and trekking for four days through the Andes to reach safety, according to a Colombian military source.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio hails Colombia's new pro-Trump leader De la Espriella on first stop of Latin American tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f57f551f3b46bf661ab90ebee300e4b8db650c3b48042fbe42f16b5311de655</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T06:27:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-hails-colombia-new-pro-trump-leader-de-la-espriella-first-stop-of-latin-american-tour--5ea929df5bfe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-hails-colombia-new-pro-trump-leader-de-la-espriella-first-stop-of-latin-american-tour" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio pledged closer security cooperation with Bogota on the first stop of his three-nation tour of pro-Washington Latin American nations. Rubio hailed the election of Colombian President Abelardo De La Espriella as part of a growing alignment with US interests across the Western Hemisphere.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US bans Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as trade spat escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53c6155a0a1abd9c62fbbf019858cc9d686f70de113e24d24ff546612f48c1f9</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T02:36:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates--c7ae8aea47d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates" /><summary type="html">The US and Canada escalated a bitter trade dispute on Tuesday, with Washington imposing new import bans on Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US goods took effect.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New York City releases post-9/11 air toxicity information kept secret for 25 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c51ba744070c86b19f03be68fb08f46fd1b437102c38703f79e8acd0ff935897</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T01:44:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years--591bfaa53874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani on Tuesday announced the release of tens of thousands of documents detailing what city officials knew about toxic air after the September 11 attacks as the 25th anniversary approaches and thousands still suffer from related illnesses.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Smithsonian chief steps down amid Trump pressure over how US history is presented</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0476398a42849f9259d2e891a26a0c4755fc8809643a0137342d1af35815276</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T00:10:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure--786389f668db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure" /><summary type="html">The Smithsonian announced Tuesday that Secretary Lonnie Bunch will leave his post at the end of the year as the institution faces continued scrutiny from the Trump administration over how its museums present US history.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Accelerating diversification: Canada seeks economic sovereignty amid Trump's 'nonsensical' posturing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9bc97eafbf3db1ed8f48ec10822647a251e67c88e7f8f59b8b37be056d07931</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:02:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-accelerating-diversification-canada-seeks-economic-sovereignty-amid-trump-s-nonsensical-pos--b741b10ffed3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-accelerating-diversification-canada-seeks-economic-sovereignty-amid-trump-s-nonsensical-posturing" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24’s François Picard speaks with Jean Simard, President and CEO of the Aluminum Association of Canada. According to Simard, the US-Canada aluminum dispute is not a conventional disagreement over trade, but rather a 'Trump posture that makes no sense". As American industrial demand substantially exceeds domestic production capacity, tariffs will do nothing to reduce Canadian aluminum from the US market. Protectionism does not eliminate interdependence, explains Simard, it makes that interdependence considerably more expensive.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump posts AI map showing US 'takeover' of North America, Iceland and Caribbean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d21d4d9fd957418b58d3324373b2256afd67ff0bc16f7fed93ad7e11662a3d</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:43:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-posts-ai-map-showing-us-takeover-of-north-america-iceland-and-caribbean-1--323e2c877033.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-posts-ai-map-showing-us-takeover-of-north-america-iceland-and-caribbean-1" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump shared an AI-generated map Monday appearing to show the US absorbing Canada, Mexico, Greenland, Iceland, Cuba and parts of the Caribbean into a giant “United States of America”. Shared without context, the post sparked diplomatic backlash. Iceland summoned its ambassador and Mexico defended its sovereignty. Denmark also pushed back over Greenland. Online, the map has triggered widespread ridicule and questions about Trump’s fitness for office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Canada will move faster from US reliance as tariffs take effect and Trump response looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:833c046448f5f99a521b1ead8155dd161c9c6d2e969974230cf24e75836428ab</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:19:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms--f0cf636eb7a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Tuesday that Canada would move faster to reduce its economic reliance on the United States as retaliatory tariffs took effect on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods and the country braced for President Donald Trump’s response. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>'US Midterm elections tend to be referendums on the unpopularity of the president'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71d69bdeb65fe655c93e8499ef1ad031a534fd6a30e72d0f460a60036275003c</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:25:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president--66d8de516e55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Michelle Swers, Professor of Government at Georgetown University. She frames the New Hampshire primary as both a major Senate contest and an unusually strong indication of the national political climate ahead of November. While Democrats face a difficult Senate map and cannot afford to surrender an open seat they already hold, the broader midterm political environment might become a referendum on President Donald Trump’s performance. New Hampshire is particularly instructive because its closely divided electorate makes national political currents more visible. Swers argues that Trump’s low approval and the local economic consequences of tariffs on Canada create significant headwinds for Republicans, especially in a state whose political identity is strongly associated with resistance to taxation.</summary></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43e12a63a5e6d356db0558fb5f36edcf7a6cd1bbd48bd5e38603c20c0b34db8f</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rubio kicks off tour in Latin America as US vies for regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:387f827cea3c8498546f1310ce411c4e2e9dd0c362ec899444c3d00291299987</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:59:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence--172a56fc9e10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence" /><summary type="html">United States Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday arrived in Colombia following the recent election of hard-right lawyer and US ally President Abelardo de la Espriella, and a string of right-wing electoral victories across Latin America. Colombia is the first stop on a tour designed to bolster pro-US leaders and cement influence over the continent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's counter-tariffs take effect on several US goods as trade war reignites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4dae2b8dd6809f2d897692ecebc2d49eed1789a054e72fdae8472f610776d64</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T04:03:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites--78ed840cdcb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites" /><summary type="html">Canada's counter-tariffs on billions of dollars in US products took effect Tuesday, as a trade war between the two countries heated up. Ottawa's pushback comes weeks after US President Donald Trump imposed 50-percent tariffs on a similar value of Canadian products, over what Washington deemed as "discriminatory treatment" against US alcohol, automobile and dairy industries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ban Canadian Bombardier jets from US market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e67d35b8c61194ca0e2a4346734d90cc6341bf4bff3e506b3f55337fbc39ddc2</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market--64decde9a947.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump threatened on Monday to block sales of Canadian planemaker Bombardier in the United States unless it builds aircraft in the country, escalating trade tensions on the eve of Canadian retaliatory tariffs. Trump accused Canada of “unjust and unfair” trade practices but did not explain how a ban would work.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
